{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542768-curseborne-the-fae","id":1542768,"title":"[Curseborne] The Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-27T07:05:51-07:00","id":1542768,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Curseborne] The Fae","content":"We've had a lot of questions about who the Fae are in Curseborne. Maybe this blog will help you out with that...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-the-fae/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-the-fae/</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T17:10:46-07:00","id":1542845,"title":"","content":"I brook this with no disrespect. But, why here? Nobody seems to be directly engaging with these posts. While you are a moderator and an in-house developer, the dead-silence and repetition of all of these gives the appearance of spam advertisement. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't head into the OwoD servers or threads and constantly promote the CofD in its threads, despite the two sharing a lot of similarities. I expect that if I did something like this, I would be banned or muted. <br /> <br /> Now. I hope I haven't prompted an engagement in hostilities, because - beyond my questioning and a possible misunderstanding of the social dynamics of this forum - I find practical issue with these posts. I - and others who have frequented this forum - tend to utilize a specific method of search to find what we are looking for. Searching by reactions.<br /> <br /> In an ideal situation, where these posts get the engagement you likely desire, would make it harder for searchers like us to find the content we want in the threads specifically designed and formatted to host such information.<br /> <br /> I am sure Curseborne is a lovely game with the excellent team who have written great works that I am familiar with - however, most people in the CofD community aren't unaware of Curseborne. I am a person aware of Curseborne who is not one yet to try it out. I particularly prefer older systems with legacies and a long-depth of answered questions and developments. Something CofD can offer me which a new system can't. <br /> <br /> I don't mean it come across as a butthole, but didn't specifically select a CofD thread to wade through posts about its spiritual successor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28571-seven-ate-nine","name":"Seven.Ate.Nine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T19:26:03-07:00","id":1542848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seven.Ate.Nine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542768-curseborne-the-fae?p=1542845#post1542845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brook this with no disrespect. But, why here? Nobody seems to be directly engaging with these posts. While you are a moderator and an in-house developer, the dead-silence and repetition of all of these gives the appearance of spam advertisement.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't head into the OwoD servers or threads and constantly promote the CofD in its threads, despite the two sharing a lot of similarities. I expect that if I did something like this, I would be banned or muted.<br /> <br /> Now. I hope I haven't prompted an engagement in hostilities, because - beyond my questioning and a possible misunderstanding of the social dynamics of this forum - I find practical issue with these posts. I - and others who have frequented this forum - tend to utilize a specific method of search to find what we are looking for. Searching by reactions.<br /> <br /> In an ideal situation, where these posts get the engagement you likely desire, would make it harder for searchers like us to find the content we want in the threads specifically designed and formatted to host such information.<br /> <br /> I am sure Curseborne is a lovely game with the excellent team who have written great works that I am familiar with - however, most people in the CofD community aren't unaware of Curseborne. I am a person aware of Curseborne who is not one yet to try it out. I particularly prefer older systems with legacies and a long-depth of answered questions and developments. Something CofD can offer me which a new system can't.<br /> <br /> I don't mean it come across as a butthole, but didn't specifically select a CofD thread to wade through posts about its spiritual successor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not seeing engagement with Curseborne on the Chronicles threads because the posting of the Curseborne information is doing what it's supposed to-getting people who might be interested in it to engage with Curseborne on the Curseborne forums and Discord. It's alerting the maybe-interested, and the interested are going where the conversations are.<br /> <br /> Also it's Onyx Path's Forums, they can do what they want with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T20:04:55-07:00","id":1542849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seven.Ate.Nine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542768-curseborne-the-fae?p=1542845#post1542845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brook this with no disrespect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You brought back a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1539153-the-primal-get-of-lyka#post1541776\">finished two-month-old argument</a> and added basically nothing new.<br /> <br /> There is a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1541260-shouldn-t-we-y-know-be-visibly-complaining-at-paradox-for-quietly-killing-chrod?p=1541305#post1541305\">case to be made</a> for supporting Curseborne being the closest route we currently have to push Paradox to start actually accepting pitches for new Chronicles books.<br /> <br /> These threads are clearly labeled and make up roughly one line of text on the list of threads on their respective boards. A thread's replies only affect its relative placement on the list of threads \u2014 a list comprised, again, of single lines of text \u2014 and its reactions are not shown in differentiated form until you open the thread to look at individual posts on account of how vBulletin only changed from Likes to Reactions about a year ago. The OPs of the threads themselves are composed of a link and one or two sentences refining on the titles. The amount to be reasonable annoyed with is negligible on account of how these posts are part of a semi-finite set of topics and are being made on a less-than-daily basis.<br /> <br /> I've been camped out on the Chronicles boards specifically since this forum was made to migrate to from the old White Wolf Forums eleven years ago, at least glancing at the contents of every single thread that's been created across all twelve boards because of personal issues with the Mark As Read button. I'm interested in the lore of Curseborne but don't feel I have enough to discuss about it pending the full release and I'm not as fond of Storypath as the Storytelling System at this point in my life, so having a way to quickly reference the currently available material without going to a different board or page through the blog posts using the main site interface is mildly useful.<br /> <br /> I've been on vBulletin forums in one form or another since I was twelve. Nobody I've ever met looks for searches by reactions to find what they're looking for, but almost all of them know how to read well enough to identify a clearly labeled topic and decide whether or not they want to engage with it from there.<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter for Curseborne is in October and it's currently late September. If you want more Chronicles content on the Chronicles board you have the tools to create threads on topics that aren't Curseborne or pull existing threads to the top of the list, but in the meantime the probable course of events is that we'll be getting distributed Curseborne posts a couple times a week for the next month or two. There are a number of other things you can do with your time if you can't tolerate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T03:31:56-07:00","id":1542862,"title":"","content":"We can see the amount of &quot;views&quot; on these, and they're not that big. _most_ responses to these threads are people going &quot;whyyy&quot;, I've even received PMs on Onyx Path. <br /> <br /> This clearly is bothering quite a few people. This clearly is negatively impacting the experience for some people.<br /> <br /> There's something to be said about community building. This is clearly a controversial topic. <br /> <br /> OPP is choosing to go with a somewhat aggressive approach of &quot;We do what we do, which is a _spammy_ post every few days&quot;. Is there really, any people reading CofD forums who yet do not know abut curseborne? Are the posts we already have not sufficient to tell new people about Curseborne? <br /> <br /> My claim and point is, that these new posts actually don't drive significant new amounts of people to Curseborne. It is souring _some_ people's opinion of OPP. And yes, this is <i>their </i>forum. <br /> <br /> But fuck, this is the first time I'm making posts on Onyx Path actually being afraid that I'll be banned for saying my opinion. <br /> <br /> This is not a good feel or a place to be. <br /> <br /> Besides this thread, which got more views do to comments, the previous 4 threads have under 30 views each. I just don't think this is in the best interest of Onyx Path. The fact that responses to such posts are basically &quot;this is a done argument, and we're proceeding as we were&quot; feels dismissive further. If it was &quot;We're actually seeing stats that these ads are worth it due to traffic they bring&quot; then I'd shut up.<br /> <br /> Even tho I said this above - forums are a community space. The way this is managed does not feel like positive community building. And that's highly disappointing. If this was any other place, and not Onyx Path, I would have left already. Onyx Path has a lot of good will built over the years, and is currently eroding it, and that would make sense if that at least brought them significant traffic, but I'm not seeing that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T06:43:19-07:00","id":1542866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542768-curseborne-the-fae?p=1542849#post1542849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You brought back a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1539153-the-primal-get-of-lyka#post1541776\">finished two-month-old argument</a> and added basically nothing new.<br /> <br /> There is a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1541260-shouldn-t-we-y-know-be-visibly-complaining-at-paradox-for-quietly-killing-chrod?p=1541305#post1541305\">case to be made</a> for supporting Curseborne being the closest route we currently have to push Paradox to start actually accepting pitches for new Chronicles books.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. There is a case to be made for it. I understand the love you possess for what OPP is doing. You've stated in an understandable format why you are okay and supportive with this matter. I appreciate that you've shared your personal experience as a reason for why this is the way it should be.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I believe there is a case to made against it. I'm not the only one who feels a type of way about this method of going about things. I am fine with OPP making their independent property. I am even fine with them using channels to advertise such matters in their CofD thread. I am less fine with the method gone about it. If OPP made a simple sticky 'Curseborne' related post-thread amongst their channels where they posted relevant updates, that would be that.<br /> <br /> However, I didn't come to potatoes section of the internet to be greeted with carrots and regarding negatively for asking what is with the bait and switch. You ask of me to tolerate it. The devs and OPP faces have asked of tolerance. This is their forum and they can do what they want with it.<br /> <br /> But am I not allowed to highlight the double standards in forum conduct I see here and speak on how I feel about it?<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">Forum Rules - Onyx Path Forums (theonyxpath.com)</a><br /> <br /> I have no disrespect with OPP. I don't have any issue with people liking Curseborne. I am not attempting to spread hate or dislike on Curseborne. But - from my perspective - these are a series of promotional posts irrelevant to the CofD I come to this particular part of the threads to look upon. If I was looking for Curseborne, there is the appropriate thread for that.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542765-curseborne-the-fae\">[Curseborne] The Fae - Onyx Path Forums (theonyxpath.com)</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> There are some points I agree with <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis\">Griautis</a></b>\u200b on the matter, but I don't wish to restate his already stated opinion again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28571-seven-ate-nine","name":"Seven.Ate.Nine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T14:27:08-07:00","id":1542880,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that people are discussing this in a civil manner. I also appreciate the reasons why some of you may not like the Curseborne posts in non-Curseborne subforums.<br /> <br /> However, these threads are incredibly easy for you to ignore if you don't want to interact with them. If they're making anyone (no matter how small the number) aware of Curseborne who hasn't previously been so, it's worth our posting in WoD and CofD spaces we control.<br /> <br /> Curseborne is a game we want and need to do well, so the potential benefit to us of attracting people who see a thread and wonder &quot;what's this about?&quot; stands to have far greater impact than requesting users who don't want to look at them to ignore them.<br /> <br /> I'm not dismissing anyone's issues here. I am explaining why it's important for us to get Curseborne under everyone's eyes, and these posts won't be getting made forever. Please have patience with us.<br /> <br /> If you don't know or care what Curseborne is, we invite you to check out curseborne.com and find out. Onyx Path doesn't currently have approval to make further Chronicles of Darkness books and only presently has approval to make the Mage: The Ascension books already on our agenda, so it may be a good game for you to look up if you like our games, our style, and want more.<br /> <br /> If you do know what Curseborne is and you don't want to get involved, please scroll past these threads. I still would appreciate you sharing the Kickstarter when it goes live, because customers allow us to keep making games. The fact that you're here means you probably like some of our work, so please help us promote Curseborne however you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T21:27:10-07:00","id":1542889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seven.Ate.Nine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542768-curseborne-the-fae?p=1542866#post1542866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But am I not allowed to highlight the double standards in forum conduct I see here and speak on how I feel about it?<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">Forum Rules - Onyx Path Forums (theonyxpath.com)</a><br /> <br /> I have no disrespect with OPP. I don't have any issue with people liking Curseborne. I am not attempting to spread hate or dislike on Curseborne. But - from my perspective - these are a series of promotional posts irrelevant to the CofD I come to this particular part of the threads to look upon. [/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll iterate again: it's Onyx Path's forums, Onyx Path can do what they want with them. Adherence to their own rules is decent community building, but it is also fundamentally a courtesy (and a rather convienent one) rather than it an obligation as it is the rest of us. More relevantly, it's just as good community building to take advantage of shared interests to direct fanbases towards a new product that will probably satisfy them-and as a bit of advertising and community building, it's working, so it'd be worse if they stopped.<br /> <br /> If you want to be rightly and properly annoyed at people doing Curseborne/Chronicles crossover threads, a long history of such makes it clear you'll be seeing a lot of people who are violating the rules for all sorts of bad reasons once the Curseborne KS is started and we have the book, and you're welcome to flag all of those posts to hell and back once they start up/<br /> <br /> But when it comes to the operations of the actual, no literally, they are on staff, not just freelancers, staff of Onyx Path on the website that they are the runners of?<br /> <br /> I'd suggest making your peace with it. Or go make your own forums, with hookers and blackjack, if that's more your speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-30-2024, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T02:46:11-07:00","id":1543051,"title":"","content":"Curseborne kickstarter is up... there's no post about it in CofD forums... :O :O<br /> <br /> Does.. does that mean OPP listened and are stopping the ads? Only bringing this up since this is <i>the </i>issue for me in terms of backing the project, when I saw the kickstater I was pleasantly surprised with the info in it, but also felt pretty bad in terms of not wanting to back it due to the ads, and so if the ads are over, that would remove the only friction I have with the project.<br /> <br /> (And hey, here's a link to the Kickstarter <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/curseborne-tabletop-roleplaying-game/description\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...me/description</a> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e"